 "answer_text": "Found 1 gene record for TP53, of 125 available: tumor protein p53 [2]. \n\nTP53 Gene Context\n\nThe encoded protein contains transcriptional activation, DNA binding, and oligomerization domains, and responds to diverse cellular stresses to regulate target genes involved in cell cycle arrest, apoptosis, senescence, DNA repair, and metabolic changes [1]. Mutations in this gene are associated with multiple human cancer types including Li-Fraumeni syndrome [1]. \n\nGene records found\n\nGene NCBIGene:7157, name: tumor protein p53 [2]. Gene symbol: TP53 [3]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: TP53 Variations in Human Cancers: New Lessons from the IARC TP53 Database and Genomics Data [4]. Pubmed title: Integrated Analysis of TP53 Gene and Pathway Alterations in The Cancer Genome Atlas [9]. Pubmed title: Specifications of the ACMG/AMP variant interpretation guidelines for germline TP53 variants [13]. Pubmed title: The Role of TP53 in Adaptation and Evolution [17]. Pubmed title: A clinical guide to TP53 mutations in myeloid neoplasms [21]. \n\nClinvar records found\n\nClinvar title: NM_000546.6(TP53):c.247G>T (p.Ala83Ser) [5]. Clinvar title: NC_000017.11:g.7666193C>T [10]. Clinvar title: NM_000546.6(TP53):c.816_864del (p.Arg273fs) [14]. Clinvar title: NM_000546.6(TP53):c.1101-73G>C [18]. Clinvar title: NM_000546.6(TP53):c.-28-3132T>C [22]. \n\nOmim records found\n\nTUMOR PROTEIN p53 [6]. TP53 [6]. \n\nGds records found\n\nGds title: Activation of the TP53 pathway is a therapeutic vulnerability in NUP98::KDM5A+ pediatric AML I [7]. Gds title: Activation of the TP53 pathway is a therapeutic vulnerability in NUP98::KDM5A+ pediatric AML II [11]. Gds title: Activation of the TP53 pathway is a therapeutic vulnerability in NUP98::KDM5A+ pediatric AML III [15]. Gds title: ATRX loss predicts poor outcomes and reveals a therapeutic vulnerability to TEAD inhibition in soft tissue sarcomas -- ATAC [19]. Gds title: ATRX loss predicts poor outcomes and reveals a t